SPIRV-Tools: the validator ends in an error, never the process or the clock

What: the library is built with C++ exceptions (CMakeLists.txt no longer adds
-fno-exceptions). assert() comes from source/omacvm/assert.h: every assert
stays in a release build and throws when it fails. Its walks that grow faster
than the module (dominator chains, depth-first traversals and the dominator
calculation, construct blocks, continue exits, the block order check,
ContainsType, the block layout check, the decoration subset checks) count
steps in source/omacvm/budget.h; every 1024th reads the thread's CPU time, and
2 s after the start the validation throws.
omacvmValidateWithOptions calls spvValidateWithOptions inside try/catch: an
exception (a failed assert, the step budget, an at() past the end,
std::bad_alloc) gives SPV_ERROR_INTERNAL and no diagnostic.
omacvmValidatorSteps says how many steps the last validation took. The
BuiltIn checks refuse a BuiltIn variable whose pointer gives no data type (an
untyped pointer) instead of reading the type id 0.
Why: Venus runs spirv-val on every guest module (virgl-venus-spirv-validate.
patch), on the thread of the guest's command ring. Fuzzed modules ended the
process inside it: ValidateImage on OpImage of an id without a type
(assert(def), compiled out by NDEBUG, then a NULL read: SIGSEGV),
CheckDecorationsFromDecoration on an OpDecorateId ArrayStrideIdEXT
(std::out_of_range; without exceptions libc++ calls abort()), and a 332-byte
module with BuiltIn SampleMask on an OpUntypedVariableKHR
(BuiltInsValidator::ValidateI32Arr read FindDef(0): SIGSEGV; valfuzz seed 104,
5 minutes in). Small modules kept it busy for long: 1000 nested loops (88 KB)
53 s, 400 of them 1.8 s, a
chain of 100000 blocks 5 s, 10000 loops in a row 7.5 s (M4, one core; the
validator's dominance test walks the dominator chain for each block of each
construct). vkr refuses such a module like one spirv-val reads as invalid,
also when refusals are only logged.
Upstream: not reported yet (drafts in work/spirv-624/build/upstream-drafts.md).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-spirv-validate.sh (spirv-corpus/refuse/
throw-*.spv and val-cfg-*.spv are refused and the process lives; every real
module passes and its steps are reported; the corpus under AddressSanitizer).

